plasma-network-health (1.0.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Destinations can be marked part-time, for hosts that are often switched
    off on purpose. When one stops answering its indicator turns blue instead
    of red and it takes no part in the overall status.
  * The colour for offline part-time hosts is configurable, defaulting to blue.
  * Help texts on the Destinations page describe the yellow state correctly.

 -- AtmanActive <kde.network.health.rxbe3@slmail.me>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 13:18:23 +0100

plasma-network-health (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Destinations now have three states: a host that answers but takes longer
    than its round-trip threshold is shown in yellow, between healthy green and
    unreachable red.
  * The maximum wait for a reply is now a setting of its own, defaulting to
    3000 ms, and no longer follows the probe interval.
  * Probes are allowed to overlap when that wait is longer than the interval,
    so a slow or unreachable destination is still probed once per interval.

 -- AtmanActive <kde.network.health.rxbe3@slmail.me>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:22:34 +0100
